# M / B001 — code-reviewer agent, dependency-guard hook, file-change hook (static analysis; not executed).

C R1 OL WF-010 | MUST | The code-reviewer agent performs an independent read-only review: Write, Edit and NotebookEdit are disallowed and it does not edit files. | delegated code review | none stated
C R2 OL WF-010 | MUST | The code-reviewer runs the code-review skill (preloaded) as the complete review procedure; scope, rule reads, checks, priorities, severity and output shape come from that skill. | delegated code review | none stated
C R3 OL WF-012 | MUST | The code-reviewer returns the findings exactly in the output format the code-review skill defines. | delegated code review | none stated
C R4 OL DEP-025 | MUST NOT (PreToolUse deny) | npm install, ci, install-test and update commands must not bypass peer-dependency resolution with --force, -f, --legacy-peer-deps, the equivalent npm config settings or npm_config_force / npm_config_legacy_peer_deps; resolve the actual compatibility problem instead. | Bash and PowerShell npm commands | none stated
C R5 OL DEP-001,DEP-003,DEP-004,DEP-005 | MUST (PostToolUse feedback) | NuGet and npm dependency changes follow the add-dependency workflow (latest stable compatible version from the registry, deprecation, vulnerability and license checks, approval gates); after a dependency-changing command or a manifest edit that touches dependencies the manifests are checked and the workflow is named. | dependency-changing commands and manifest edits | none stated
C R6 OL ARC-001 | MUST (PostToolUse feedback) | Project references follow .claude/rules/architecture.md (Project References); after a reference-changing command the manifests are checked and the rule is named. | .NET project reference commands | none stated
C R7 OL GOV-021,GOV-009 | SHOULD (PostToolUse reminder) | When CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md changes, run the custom-settings workflow to synchronize every affected surface and confirm it stays consistent with SPECIFICATION.md. | edits of CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md | none stated
C R8 OL GOV-009,GOV-007 | SHOULD (PostToolUse reminder) | When SPECIFICATION.md changes, confirm it stays consistent with CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md and carry approved behavior changes through the development-workflow. | edits of SPECIFICATION.md | none stated
C X1 EX ARC-020,ARC-001,GOV-017 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL (Reserved; PostToolUse routing) | A changed production project reference graph, including a removed project file, is a Reserved decision that goes through Decision Control. | .NET project references and project files | Already required by the specification or established project structure. | ARC-020 requires approval for new layers/projects and ARC-001 constrains direction; no oracle policy makes individual reference edges or project removal Reserved. | Adding a reference between two existing projects needs a Decision Request.
C X2 EX GOV-017,ARC-020 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | For an unclear decision, any 'yes' to five questions makes it Reserved: does it add, remove or replace a dependency, framework or infrastructure capability; change a project, layer or reference boundary; establish a convention other code is expected to follow; change observable behavior or a public contract; or would it be expensive to reverse once other code depends on it. | decision classification | none stated | GOV-017 defines Decided/Delegated/Reserved classes; the oracle does not provide a test that turns any of these properties into a Reserved decision. | Removing an unused package or a package-version file becomes Reserved under the test.
C X3 EX DEP-001 | MUST | Dependency removals follow the add-dependency workflow like additions and updates. | NuGet and npm dependency removals | none stated | DEP-001..DEP-005 govern additions and updates; no oracle policy routes removals through the dependency workflow. | Uninstalling a package without the add-dependency steps does not follow the instruction.

